            <h2>Airlines Flying from San Diego to Boston</h2>
            <p>Five carriers operate nonstop or connecting service between San Diego and Boston: JetBlue Airways, Alaska Airlines, Southwest Airlines, Delta Air Lines, and American Airlines.</p>
            <h3>JetBlue Airways</h3>
            <p>JetBlue leads this transcontinental route with the most daily nonstops and a product built for long-haul comfort.</p>
            <p><b>Highlights:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Multiple daily nonstops to Boston aboard Airbus A320 family and A220 aircraft</li>
                <li>The most legroom in coach among major domestic carriers</li>
                <li>Free high-speed Wi-Fi, live TV, and complimentary snacks and soft drinks at every seat</li>
                <li>TrueBlue points earning with no blackout dates and family pooling</li>
                <li>Mint business-class lie-flat seats on select rotations for premium transcontinental comfort</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Alaska Airlines</h3>
            <p>The West Coast's hometown carrier brings its award-winning service and loyalty program to this cross-country corridor.</p>
            <p><b>Highlights:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Daily nonstop service to Boston aboard Boeing 737 aircraft</li>
                <li>Atmos Rewards earning with valuable elite status and partner redemptions</li>
                <li>Complimentary elite upgrades when available, plus premium extra legroom</li>
                <li>Seamless connections from dozens of West Coast cities through San Diego</li>
                <li>Seasonal fares from $119 in off-peak months</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Southwest Airlines (Low-Cost)</h3>
            <p>Southwest brings its value-driven model to this route with a new red-eye option that maximizes East Coast time.</p>
            <p><b>Features:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Daily nonstop red-eye service between SAN and BOS aboard Boeing 737 MAX 8 aircraft, launching June 4, 2026</li>
                <li>Rapid Rewards points with no blackout dates and fully refundable flexibility.</li>
                <li>Two free checked bags on every fare - a rarity on transcontinental routes</li>
                <li>No change fees; pay only the fare difference if plans shift</li>
                <li>Overnight timing allows a full final day in San Diego and an early arrival in Boston</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Delta Air Lines</h3>
            <p>Delta connects San Diego to Boston through its Salt Lake City and Atlanta hubs, with occasional seasonal nonstops.</p>
            <p><b>Advantages:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Daily connecting service via Salt Lake City and Atlanta, with seasonal nonstop options.</li>
                <li>SkyMiles earning with Medallion elite benefits and upgrade priority</li>
                <li>Free Wi-Fi for SkyMiles members on equipped aircraft</li>
                <li>Delta Sky Club access at SAN Terminal 2 for eligible passengers</li>
                <li>Industry-leading operational reliability</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>American Airlines</h3>
            <p>American links San Diego to Boston through its Dallas/Fort Worth and Charlotte hubs, backed by the world's largest loyalty program.</p>
            <p><b>Benefits:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Connecting service to Boston via Dallas/Fort Worth and Charlotte</li>
                <li>AAdvantage mileage earning with Loyalty Points toward elite status</li>
                <li>Main Cabin Extra legroom and premium cabins on transcontinental rotations</li>
                <li>Admirals Club access at SAN Terminal 2 for eligible passengers</li>
                <li>Extensive domestic and international feed enabling complex itineraries</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Connecting Options</h3>
            <p>One-stop itineraries route through Denver, Salt Lake City, Dallas/Fort Worth, Chicago, Charlotte, Phoenix, and Atlanta, often priced below nonstops. Frontier Airlines offers ultra-low-cost connecting service for budget-conscious travelers.</p>
            <h2>Seasonal Variations</h2>
            <h3>Peak Season: Mid-June through August, Mid-October through November, Mid-December through Early January</h3>
            <p>The route's high seasons combine summer tourism, fall foliage pilgrimages, and holiday travel.</p>
            <p><b>During peak months:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Airfares reach annual highs, with Thanksgiving week and Christmas commanding the steepest premiums</li>
                <li>Summer brings peak demand for Cape Cod, Martha's Vineyard, and Nantucket access via Boston</li>
                <li>Fall foliage season from late September through October draws leaf-peepers to New England's countryside</li>
                <li>Hotel rates in Boston climb with minimum-stay requirements; historic inns and harbor hotels book out weeks ahead</li>
                <li>College move-in weekends in late August and early September create secondary fare spikes</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Shoulder Season: Late April through Early June, September through Mid-October</h3>
            <p>The sweet spot for value, weather, and manageable crowds.</p>
            <p><b>Advantages:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Economy fares typically run 20 to 30 percent below peak levels</li>
                <li>Spring blooms along the Charles River Esplanade and comfortable walking weather</li>
                <li>Shoulder-season hotel deals and easier reservations at Boston's renowned restaurants</li>
                <li>Better upgrade availability and award seat inventory across all carriers</li>
                <li>The Head of the Charles Regatta in October and Boston Marathon registration season</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Off-Peak Value Windows: January through Early March</h3>
            <p>Post-holiday and pre-spring weeks deliver the cheapest fares of the year.</p>
            <p><b>Benefits:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>January is historically the cheapest month, with round trips averaging near $282</li>
                <li>Uncrowded museums, shorter lines at the USS Constitution, and easier Freedom Trail access</li>
                <li>Winter restaurant week deals and post-holiday hotel promotions</li>
                <li>World-class skiing within two hours at Vermont and New Hampshire resorts</li>
            </ul>
            <p><b>Considerations:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Boston winters are genuinely cold, with temperatures frequently in the 20s°F and significant snowfall</li>
                <li>Nor'easters can disrupt Northeast air operations; travel insurance is strongly recommended</li>
                <li>Some outdoor attractions and harbor islands operate reduced winter hours</li>
            </ul>
